course: dictionary
lesson: 1855
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word code has more than one meaning. Use the words around it to choose the right one. «Ruby in Perth watched her big brother type his phone code» means a number that unlocks a phone, not a secret message.
explain: A code can be a system of letters, numbers or signs used to send secret messages. Code can also mean the instructions a computer follows, and coding is writing them. A code can also be a set of rules, like a dress code.
explain: Ask what the word is doing in the sentence. Is it a number that unlocks something, a set of rules, or a message nobody else can read? Then try your meaning in the sentence to check that it makes sense.
fact: A code is a system of letters, numbers or signs used to send secret messages.
fact: Coding means writing instructions for a computer.
fact: A code can be a number or letters used to unlock something, like a PIN code or a postcode.
fact: A «dress code» is a set of rules about what to wear.
fact: Never share your PIN code or passwords with anyone.
exercise: «Ruby in Perth watched her big brother type his phone code.» In this sentence, what does code mean? | A dance for the school show | A set of rules for a team | *A number used to unlock something
exercise: Mia writes instructions that tell a computer to draw a square. What is she doing? | Breaking a code | *Coding | Dressing up for a party
exercise: «Each kind of firefly has its own flash code.» What is a flash code most like? | A type of shoe | *A pattern of light signals, like Morse code | A sleepy beetle
test: What is the safest thing to do with your PIN code? | Share it with a friend | *Keep it secret | Write it on the keypad
test: How many possible 4-digit PIN codes are there? | *10,000 | 100,000 | 100 | 1,000
exam: Which meaning of code fits «The school has a strict dress code»? | A secret message | A number to unlock a door | *A set of rules | Instructions for a computer
